# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repo grew with core.autocrlf=true and no attribute file, so the index mixes
# LF and CRLF.  These rules stop that from spreading (new files are normalised)
# without rewriting history or mass-renormalising existing blobs -- a one-shot
# `git add --renormalize .` would otherwise show up as a whitespace-only diff
# across a dozen files.  Run it later if you want the tree fully consistent.
* text=auto

# Shell/Python tooling in this repo is executed on Linux/WSL, where a stray CR
# breaks the shebang and `bash -e` line.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf

# Windows-only launchers keep their native endings.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Generated protobuf stubs: never diff, never merge.
nanovllm/serving/nanovllm_pb2.py      -diff merge=binary
nanovllm/serving/nanovllm_pb2_grpc.py -diff merge=binary

# Binary/archive material.
*.png   binary
*.out   -text diff
*.log   -text diff
